<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The system splash's colours.

        They cannot come from the chosen palette: the framework reads this
        theme before any of the app's code runs, so there is nothing to ask.
        What they can do is get out of the way. Every palette's own background
        is its primary mixed 90% into white, which lands between #ECF8F7 and
        #FFF7E6 — so a near-neutral here is within a couple of shades of
        whichever one the user has, and the hand-off to the Compose animation
        underneath it is not visible.

        The glyph is the app's ink for the same reason: neutral sits with any
        palette, where a fixed brand colour would clash with half of them.
    -->
    <color name="splash_background">#F4F6F7</color>
    <color name="splash_glyph">#1A1C1E</color>
</resources>
